  "narrative": "No claim is accepted at this appraise stage. I judged the 12 new results against scale-aware 10% clinical benchmarks: approximately outcome_013 0.0269, outcome_008 0.0282, outcome_011 0.0301, outcome_006 0.0175, and outcome_014 0.0093. H47, H54, and H58 are directional claims whose signed intervals either lie mostly opposite or have upper confidence bounds far below the corresponding clinical threshold, so they do not support clinically meaningful stronger dependency and are closed. H49 is especially informative against the original stronger-dependency hypothesis: the signed estimate is negative with a 95% interval entirely below zero, indicating the opposite direction, so H49 is rejected and closed. I am not currently proposing a reversed claim because the reversed lower bound would still not clearly exceed the clinical threshold and the feature_042 pattern is discordant overall. The feature_042 follow-ups also failed to produce a coherent pattern: outcome_013 and outcome_011 are near null, the outcome_006/feature_030 interaction is extremely imprecise, and the strongest earlier outcome_006 main effect already failed independent validation. The feature_034 follow-ups are mostly small or null; H54 rules out the stronger-dependency direction for outcome_013, while other outcomes remain too weak or imprecise to pursue. The feature_060 follow-ups are similar, except H55 is the closest candidate: outcome_006 has a point estimate above the 0.0175 threshold, but its interval includes zero and therefore does not support acceptance or validation yet. I therefore request no independent validation in this round and will prioritize remaining high-power untested main effects, especially feature_002 and feature_047 extensions, before spending validation on any borderline signal.",
