  "narrative": "No new validation result or assessment deadline was delivered in this synthesis stage, so I changed no claim statuses on evidence grounds. The supported finding set remains empty under the stated clinical criterion. Using a conservative scale-aware interpretation of a 10% or greater clinically meaningful difference in dependency score, no comparison currently has a lower confidence bound above the relevant threshold, and the strongest prior feature_042 signal failed independent validation and does not have a coherent multi-outcome follow-up pattern. The closed negative findings are informative: several predictors show intervals incompatible with clinically meaningful stronger dependency, and the outcome_008/feature_042 comparison is robustly in the opposite direction. I do not accept a reversed feature_042/outcome_008 claim because the reversed lower confidence bound remains below the clinical threshold and the broader feature_042 pattern is inconsistent. The main unresolved uncertainty is in borderline or low-power main effects, especially H55, whose point estimate exceeds the outcome_006 threshold but whose interval includes zero and therefore does not justify acceptance or validation. The next analysis wave should prioritize the registered high-precision feature_002 and feature_047 comparisons H59-H65. If those are null, close these predictor lines and move toward broader categorical or continuous predictor screening, reserving validation for effects whose uncertainty intervals support clinically meaningful differences rather than merely large point estimates. Any accepted conclusion would still be dataset-specific association evidence, not causal or generalizable.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted set: none. No new validation arrived in this synthesis stage. H23/R25 remains the only independent validation evidence and does not support acceptance. Feature_042 remains deprioritized: H19 and H21 are unresolved positive discovery signals, but H23 failed validation and follow-ups are incoherent, with H49 robustly opposite. Feature_034 is deprioritized after null or weak multi-outcome results. Feature_060 has only the borderline H55 outcome_006 signal, which is unresolved because the interval includes zero. Next priority: analyze H59-H65, covering feature_002 on outcome_006/outcome_014/outcome_013/outcome_008/outcome_011 and feature_047 on outcome_006/outcome_014. If these are null, close or defer those balanced binary lines and allocate discovery toward untested categorical predictors or continuous contrasts, not further feature_042 or feature_034 main effects unless subgroup-specific evidence appears. Validation policy: do not validate borderline point estimates with lower bounds far below clinical thresholds; validate only when an interval supports a clinically meaningful difference or when there is a strong coherent multi-outcome pattern needing replication. Scale-aware approximate 10% absolute-mean thresholds: outcome_001 0.0415, outcome_006 0.0175, outcome_013 0.0269, outcome_014 0.0093, outcome_008 0.0282, outcome_011 0.0301."
